[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Want to keep your subject in the frame?&nbsp; In this video, we\'ll walk you through&nbsp;&nbsp; the basics of smart tracking so you can track&nbsp; with ease and focus on filming. Autotracking. While recording, push the joystick&nbsp; in once to enable autotracking,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and the camera will automatically&nbsp; lock on to the subject in frame. While active, move the joystick to manually&nbsp; adjust the subject\'s framing in the shot. Tap anywhere outside the tracked subject on the&nbsp; screen or push the joystick in again to cancel&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tracking. In addition, press and hold the joystick&nbsp; to automatically enable group tracking depending&nbsp;&nbsp; on the number of people in the frame. It ensures&nbsp; all subjects are properly framed in group shots&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'without the need for manual refframing,&nbsp; significantly simplifying group shooting.&nbsp;&nbsp; You can also enable tracking in two other ways.&nbsp;&nbsp; One, double tap the subject you&nbsp; want to track on the touch screen.&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[00:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Two, tap the screen icon to enable autotracking.&nbsp; Then tap or draw a box to select the subject.&nbsp;&nbsp; The camera will quickly lock onto and track the&nbsp; selected object or person. Thanks for watching&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[01:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Luna Ultra autotracking guide. Stay tuned&nbsp; for more tutorials from us. See you next time.'
